    "title": "Body recovered from Wood Dale/Itasca Reservoir - NewsBreak",
    "text": "WOOD DALE, Ill. ( WGN ) — A dead body was recovered from a reservoir in DuPage County Wednesday night, according to police. The Forest Preserve District of DuPage County police said they recovered the body of a missing individual around 7:35 p.m. while searching the Wood Dale/Itasca Reservoir by kayak. Authorities have yet to identify the body. 52-year-old Hipolito Hernandez vanished Tuesday evening at a spot in the reservoir where swimming is banned. He was with his girlfriend and tried to swim across the reservoir when he disappeared. DuPage County officials said the reservoir can get up to 40 feet deep, but according to search teams, the water level was as low as four feet deep Wednesday morning. The DuPage County Coroner’s Office, led by Coroner Judith Lukas, will work to identify the individual and determine the official cause of death. The Forest Preserve District of DuPage County Police is continuing its investigation. The forest preserve will resume normal operating hours Thursday morning. No other information is available at this time. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WGN-TV.",
